From 293ae1d698ea33fdda11adc659dd5299d1fada41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:29:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH milos-linux v1 3/3] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Align Milos RDI
 lines to 16 bytes
To: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>

The TFE on Milos writes RDI data in 128-bit bus words (downstream
TFE665 rdi_width = 128, and its RAW10 line-mode calculation aligns
width * 10 bits to that width). camss defaults to 8-byte line alignment,
so for widths that are not a multiple of 16 bytes the negotiated
bytesperline does not match what the hardware writes.

Add CAMSS_MILOS to the group of SoCs that use 16-byte alignment. On the
Fairphone 6 the front 3104x2336 RAW10 mode gets a stride of 3888 bytes
(sizeimage 0x8a9600) and streams correctly; the rear sensors' strides
(5120 and 1712) are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index fb7ee2fcb2f1..908fa75b8317 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -2014,6 +2014,8 @@ static int vfe_bpl_align_rdi(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 	case CAMSS_8550:
 	case CAMSS_8650:
 	case CAMSS_8775P:
+	/* TFE665 writes RDI data in 128-bit bus words. */
+	case CAMSS_MILOS:
 	case CAMSS_X1E80100:
 		ret = 16;
 		break;
